          <Pad Id="orztv7n95UUMR6Vmi83jZo" Bounds="85,870,1049,400" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xA;- The nodes appear when the qml folder exists next to the saved patch, or in the qml folder of a package; subfolders count. Only files whose name starts with an uppercase letter become nodes (QML's rule for components): main.qml or helpers are skipped. Middle click on the node opens the file.&#xA;- Pins come only from the declarations of the root object: property (input, plus an optional output with the last value QML changed), readonly property (output), signal (output). Types: real, int, bool, string, color, vector2d/3d/4d, point, size, rect, url (Path), date (DateTime), font (Font, size in units like Text), and list&lt;…&gt; of these but font (Spread pins). The other pins are those of QmlElement (see HowTo Use a QML file).&#xA;- A pin sends nothing until its value differs from the declared default: a binding or an initial value in the file stays in charge until you really set the pin.&#xA;- Save the .qml and the running element reloads. The pins change only when the declarations change (a new, renamed or retyped property or signal, a default, the comment above it, a head tag); links on pins with the same name stay.&#xA;- A list&lt;T&gt; property is a Spread pin: list&lt;point&gt; and list&lt;size&gt; take a Spread of Vector2 (Points of TrendCard: X is the time, Y the value), list&lt;string&gt; a Spread of String (Labels). A literal array in the file is the default, otherwise the default is an empty Spread; the pin sends once its content differs from it. At most 65536 elements.&#xA;- property alias name: id.prop gets the pin of the target's type: a property a child declares, a known property of a built-in type (Text text and color, Rectangle color and radius, Image source, size, position, opacity, scale and visible of every Item), or a root property of a component of the same folder. An enum of the root gives no pin of its own; a property of its type or with one of its values (ProfileCard.Online) is an int pin whose help lists the values.&#xA;- An alias the parser cannot resolve (of a whole object, of border.color), var, object properties and lists of other types (lists of lists, of objects) get no pin (info at the node). Set them through the hidden Properties pin, the dictionary of QmlElement (plan B).&#xA;- A file that does not parse still gives a node: parser messages show at the node, QML errors at the node and in the log.&#xA;- Full and Milestone 100 stay silent here: the LFO ramp falls back to 0 before the animated bar (Behavior, 400 ms) reaches 100 %. Set Value to 1 and they fire. Signals report what QML emits, nothing is lost on the way.&#xA;- Export: the qml folder next to the exported patch is copied next to the exe.&#xA;- Experimental, like QmlElement.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="CoreLibBasics.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
